2026-09-27 — explicit continuations for long arithmetic expressions

RED: inline-deep-expression.c expands to 600 left-associated additions inside
the recursive visitor reduction. Parsing succeeds, but a normal debug driver
aborts on host stack overflow in --interpret-c-hir, --interpret-evoir and
--emit=asm. The release compiler already executes this bounded case; this is
compiler/debug robustness, not a claim of a previously wrong kernel value.

Successive macOS crash reports identify actual recursion, not a guessed stack
limit: Substitution::expr, Interpreter::predeclare_expr, recursive scalar
Interpreter::eval_expr/eval_binary, and FunctionLowerer::lower_expr/lower_binary.
Reports are evocc-2026-09-27-213355/214538/214539/215217/215448/215630.ips in
~/Library/Logs/DiagnosticReports. No debugger transcript is claimed.

Repair:
  * Carry ordinary binary left-spine rewrite/lowering continuations explicitly.
    Preserve original constant admission, left-before-right traversal, memo
    bookkeeping and the existing per-node binary/type/UB tail.
  * Discover expression-local declarations using an explicit structural stack.
  * Use the existing C-HIR task machine for composite scalar expressions instead
    of the recursive no-call shortcut; retain only leaf fast paths.
  * Keep logical operators' selected-path handling and existing explicit local
    SSA transport when a right operand opens CFG edges.
No stack-limit increase, source whitelist, new IR operation or UB suppression.
This does not assert that all arbitrary AST nesting is now stack-independent.

Focused CLI group: 11 PASS, O0/O2, both interpreters and assembly emission.
The second long-chain test exercises a conditional RHS with ++/-- on a distinct
local, selected effects, skipped divide-by-zero branches and an actually reached
division by zero (E3002). Previous admission/lifetime/E3001/E3002 controls remain.
No unsequenced multiple modifications are used as an oracle.

Native: the unchanged long-expression and recursive-visitor fixtures both exit
zero under GCC14 / Clang19 / EvoCC at O0/O2: 12 PASS. The later selected-effects
control is a CLI/interpreter/assembly test, not an extra native execution.
